.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.CREATETHEAD" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.createTHead \- HTMLTableElement: createTHead() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]createTHead()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface creates a \f[CR]<thead>\f[R]
element, inserts it before the first element child of the given
\f[CR]<table>\f[R] that\(cqs neither a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] nor a
\f[CR]<colgroup>\f[R], or as the last child if no such insertion
location is found, and returns it.
If the table already has a \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element child, this method
returns the first such child without creating one.
.PP
When creation is needed, this method creates and inserts the element
directly, without requiring separate calls to methods such as
\f[CR]Document.createElement()\f[R] and \f[CR]Node.insertBefore()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createTHead()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
An \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R] (which is always a
\f[CR]thead\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] myHead = myTable.createTHead();
\f[I]// Now this should be true: myHead === myTable.tHead\f[R]
.EE
